Upstream candidate for better-auth/better-auth (packages/oauth-provider).
Keys refresh-token reuse detection and revocation on grant lineage
(oauthRefreshToken.authorizationCodeId) instead of (clientId, userId), stamps
device grants with lineage device:<deviceCode.id>, and refuses a refresh row
without a lineage. Revoking a live refresh token ends its lineage, including
access tokens earlier rotations issued (RFC 7009 section 2.1). A refresh token
keeps the grant's scopes rather than the scopes left after intersecting with
the requested resources, so a refresh for one audience does not narrow the
grant for the others (RFC 8707: only the access token is audience-restricted).
ADR-0549. Re-verify on every Better Auth upgrade.

